# Alice (seat 0, human) holds Thirst for Knowledge
# ({3}{U}, "Draw three cards. Then discard two cards unless you discard an
# artifact card.") and four untapped Islands — enough to cast it with nothing
# to respond. No artifact anywhere in her hand or on her battlefield, so the
# card's "unless" clause is never live and the discard is always the plain
# "choose two of your hand" choice.
#
# Measured against the real jar: that discard reaches the wire as a
# `setSelectables` (`min:2, max:2`), never a blocking ask. Two Mountains
# already in hand, plus three more drawn off the top of the library, give her
# FIVE lands to choose two of after the spell leaves her hand — a real choice
# (ten distinct two-card subsets), not the single legal answer the server's
# own "one option" shortcut would auto-collapse (`thoughtseize.state`'s own
# note on why its discarder's hand needs two different nonland cards, not
# one). Bob (seat 1) holds nothing of his own; he is only here to watch
# alice's open ask on his own banner.
